# deploy/hearth.env.example — environment for the Hearth container in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml.
#
# Usage:
#   cp deploy/hearth.env.example deploy/hearth.env    # then edit
#   chmod 600 deploy/hearth.env
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
#
# deploy/hearth.env is gitignored. The compose file marks it `required: true`:
# the container runs in production mode, which cannot start without the two
# keys below.
#
# SCOPE — this file is read by ONE service, so it holds only that service's
# keys. Compose injects every key here into the container's runtime
# environment, where `docker inspect` can read them. Do not put credentials for
# anything other than Hearth in it, and do not point compose at the repository
# root .env: audit 2026-08-28 §4.8#17. scripts/check-compose-env-scope.sh fails
# the build if a key outside this scope appears here.
#
# HOW THESE VALUES REACH HEARTH — there is no generic "env overrides
# hearth.yaml" mechanism. A variable here does one of two things:
#   1. It is one of the few variables the server reads directly
#      (HEARTH_MASTER_KEY, HEARTH_KEK, HEARTH_PREVIOUS_MASTER_KEY,
#      HEARTH_TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY,
#      HEARTH_MAILCATCHER_PASSWORD, RUST_LOG), or
#   2. hearth.yaml references it with ${VAR} substitution, e.g.
#        email:
#          smtp:
#            password: "${HEARTH_SMTP_PASSWORD}"
#      In production an unset or empty ${VAR} is a hard start-up error.
# Anything else is ignored. Settings such as the bind address or port belong
# in hearth.yaml (the compose file already passes `--bind 0.0.0.0`). The
# compose file's own `environment:` block wins over this file for the same key.
# See docs/specs/CONFIGURATION.md for the full key reference.

# REQUIRED — storage host key: 64 hex chars (openssl rand -hex 32). Back it up
# outside this host: without it the data in the hearth_data volume is
# unreadable. Never change it on an existing volume (rotation uses
# HEARTH_PREVIOUS_MASTER_KEY; see docs/guides/security-hardening.md).
HEARTH_MASTER_KEY=

# REQUIRED — key-encryption key for realm signing keys: 64 hex chars
# (openssl rand -hex 32). Back it up alongside the master key.
HEARTH_KEK=

# SMTP password, when hearth.yaml references ${HEARTH_SMTP_PASSWORD}.
# HEARTH_SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Log filter. Overrides the compose default of "info"; RUST_LOG also takes
# priority over observability.log_level in hearth.yaml.
# RUST_LOG=info

# Readiness probe URL used by the image's healthcheck. Set the https:// form
# when hearth.yaml configures direct TLS (server.tls_cert_path).
# HEARTH_HEALTHCHECK_URL=https://127.0.0.1:8420/readyz
